  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="72">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 72</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-g-a">And þær se bonda sæt uncwydd ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wif ⁊ þa cild on þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ylcan unbesacan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-a">And þær se bonda sæt uncwyd ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif ⁊ þa cild on þam ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-q">Et ubi bónda (id est paterfamilias) mansit sine compellatione et calumpnia, sint uxor et pueri in eodem sine querela.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="72" corresp="#wit-b">And ðær se bunda sæt uncwyd [his deig] ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif ⁊ ða cild [on þam ylcan] unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And when a householder has dwelt all his time free from claims and charges, his wife and children shall dwell [on the same property] unmolested by litigation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wo der freie Hausvater unangesprochen und unbeklagt (sein Lebtag B) gesessen hat, auf demselben [Hofe] sitze unbestritten die Ehefrau und die Kinder.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And where the free householder has sat unchallenged and unaccused (all his life, B), on that same [homestead] let the wife and the children sit undisputed.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Atr 14.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
